The dma-buf capability on LikeOS.

The generic screen-capability helper asks the kernel about PRIME dma-buf
support (drmGetCap DRM_CAP_PRIME) only on the systems it has heard of;
everywhere else the block is compiled out and caps->dmabuf stays 0.  On
LikeOS the kernel answers the query (import|export = 3), but with the
capability reported as absent GBM routed every buffer through its dumb
fallback -- which accepts only CURSOR+ARGB8888 and SCANOUT+XRGB8888 -- so
the glamor front buffer (ARGB8888, SCANOUT|RENDERING) failed with EINVAL
and the X server died in ScreenInit with nothing in any log.  The device,
the kernel and the format capabilities were all willing; the query was
never made.

